---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Climb">
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Climb Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>How Climb collects, uses, and protects your information</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-doc">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="legal-doc-body">
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: July 28, 2026</p>

        <p class="legal-lede">
          Climb is a free-to-play sports prediction game by R&amp;L Labs. There is
          no real-money wagering, no prizes, and no redemption of any kind &mdash;
          picks risk only in-game rating points.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Account.</strong> You sign in with Apple or with Discord. From
          Apple we receive a private user identifier and, if you share it, your
          email address. From Discord we receive your Discord account identifier,
          username, email address, and avatar. You choose a Climb username; you
          may add a display name, an avatar photo, and a bio.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Gameplay.</strong> Your picks, results, rating (MMR), rank
          history, badges, and season standings. This is the game &mdash; public
          leaderboards and feeds show your username, avatar, rank, and picks
          unless you set your profile to private.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Social activity.</strong> Follows, blocks, reports, reactions,
          comments, and captions you post. Comments and captions are screened by
          automated moderation (including OpenAI's moderation service, which
          processes the text you submit) and may be reviewed by us when reported.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Device.</strong> A push-notification token if you allow
          notifications, and your app version, so results can reach your device.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Referrals.</strong> If you join through another player's share
          link and redeem their code, we link your account to theirs so their
          "players recruited" count works. That link is visible to us, not to
          other players.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Purchases.</strong> If you subscribe to Premium, Apple processes
          the payment. We receive and store the subscription's status (never your
          payment details) to unlock Premium features.
        </p>

        <h2>What we don't do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            We do not track you across other companies' apps or websites, and we
            do not use advertising identifiers. Ads (for free accounts) are served
            by Google AdMob in <strong>non-personalized mode</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>We do not sell your data.</li>
          <li>
            There is no real-money gambling, and no way to convert anything in
            Climb into money.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Supabase</strong> hosts our database and authentication.</li>
          <li><strong>Apple</strong> handles sign-in, payments, and push delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Discord</strong> handles sign-in when you choose it.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google AdMob</strong> serves non-personalized ads; its
            processing is described in Google's privacy policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>OpenAI</strong> screens submitted comment/caption text for
            policy violations.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You can delete your account in the app (You &rarr; Edit &rarr; Delete
          account). Deletion removes your name, picture, profile details, follows,
          notifications, device tokens, and social posts, and permanently
          anonymizes your account. Your past picks and finished-season standings
          remain on the ladder under an anonymous name so completed seasons aren't
          rewritten; they are no longer connected to you.
        </p>

        <h2>Age</h2>
        <p>
          Climb contains simulated gambling and is intended for users 18 and older.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions or requests:
          <a href="mailto:support@rl-labs.org">support@rl-labs.org</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
